  "routeAdjustment": "Reuse the original coefficient-map composition and rational-generator invariance, existing uniqueness of normalized discrete order and actual residue-field bijectivity. Native Finsupp domain equivalences, quotient functoriality and ZMod linearization supply divisor and torsion actions. A generic semilinear automorphism framework and unused field-action packaging are avoided. The inspected external stabilizer proof supplies a next route through finite function fields of definition and separation of a finite place orbit; its continuity conclusion is not yet imported or claimed.",
  "discharged": "The literal arithmetic coefficient automorphism preserves the original modular function field, fixes its rational j coordinate and transforms constants by the original field automorphism. It permutes the actual normalized places with the exact order equation. The induced additive divisor action preserves degree over algebraically closed constants and carries principal divisors to genuine transformed function divisors. It therefore descends to the actual degree-zero divisor classes, with proved group action laws, and restricts to their genuine n-torsion. Native ZMod scalar multiplication gives the actual arithmetic Galois representation on this original torsion group. No arithmetic action or place/order compatibility premise is supplied.",
  "remaining": "The actual torsion group still requires finiteness and continuous arithmetic action, followed by Tate realization, the rank-two Hecke component and Frobenius/inertia comparison for the normalized cusp eigensystem. Arithmetic automorphy and higher symmetric-power continuation remain open. DUB-17--20 OPEN; 16/20. No acceptance gate closes here.",
